# React UI

- React owns semantic UI, panels, menus, tooltips, accessibility surfaces, and settings.
- Subscribe to compact read models and selectors, not the full mutable world.
- Never update React on every Phaser frame.
- Never render individual battlefield soldiers as components.
- Convert UI intent into commands; do not directly mutate simulation state.
- Preserve keyboard operation, visible focus, labels, and non-color cues.
- Clean up worker/event subscriptions in effects.
- Keep components focused; extract domain logic into testable non-React functions.
